          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Are Partial &amp; Complete Dentures?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Losing multiple or all teeth makes chewing home-cooked meals difficult, affects clear speech, and causes cheeks and lips to sink inward. Dentures are custom-made removable sets of artificial teeth resting comfortably on the gums. Partial dentures replace a few missing teeth alongside natural ones, while complete dentures restore a full upper or lower arch for elderly patients.
          </p>
